Data Portability Export in Machine-Readable Format
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Identify which user data fields qualify as "portable" under GDPR Article 20
Build a Python script that exports user data into JSON and CSV formats
Sign an export file with GPG to guarantee its integrity
Transfer the export using SFTP on a local machine
Validate the exported JSON against a schema
Prerequisites
Basic Python knowledge (variables, functions, dictionaries)
Basic Linux command line familiarity (cd, ls, running scripts)
No prior GDPR or cryptography experience needed
Estimated time: 45-60 minutes
Environment Setup
You are provided a single Linux machine (via Start Lab). All work happens locally — no cloud accounts needed.

Open a terminal on your lab machine.
Install required packages:
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y python3 python3-pip gnupg openssh-server
pip3 install jsonschema
Create a working directory:
mkdir ~/data-portability-lab
cd ~/data-portability-lab
Task 1: Identify Portable Fields in a Sample Database
We will use a simple SQLite-like sample stored as a Python dictionary to keep things beginner-friendly.

Create a file named sample_data.py:
nano sample_data.py
Paste this sample user record (includes both portable and non-portable fields):
# sample_data.py
# This simulates a row from a user database.

USER_RECORD = {
    "user_id": "U1001",
    "full_name": "Aisha Al Farsi",           # Portable - provided by user
    "email": "aisha@example.com",            # Portable - provided by user
    "phone": "+971500000000",                # Portable - provided by user
    "signup_date": "2023-01-15",             # Portable - provided by user
    "preferences": {"newsletter": True},      # Portable - provided by user
    "internal_risk_score": 0.82,             # NOT portable - internal analytics
    "admin_notes": "VIP customer"            # NOT portable - internal use only
}
GDPR Article 20 only covers data the user provided — not data the company derived internally.
Portable: full_name, email, phone, signup_date, preferences
Not portable: internal_risk_score, admin_notes
