Task 3: Sign the Export with GPG
Generate a GPG key (if you don't have one):
gpg --full-generate-key
# Choose defaults, use any name/email, set a passphrase you will remember
List your key to confirm it exists:
gpg --list-keys
Sign the JSON export to guarantee integrity (detached signature):
gpg --output export.json.sig --detach-sign export.json
Verify the signature:
gpg --verify export.json.sig export.json
You should see "Good signature" in the output.

Task 4: SFTP Delivery (Local)
We simulate secure delivery using the local SSH/SFTP server.

Ensure SSH service is running:
sudo systemctl status ssh
sudo systemctl start ssh
Connect via SFTP to your own machine (localhost):
sftp localhost
Inside the SFTP prompt, upload the files:
put export.json
put export.json.sig
put export.csv
exit
Confirm files exist in your home directory:
ls -la ~/export.json ~/export.json.sig ~/export.csv
