Troubleshooting
"command not found: gpg" — reinstall with sudo apt install gnupg
SFTP connection refused — run sudo systemctl start ssh and retry
jsonschema import error — run pip3 install jsonschema again, check pip3 list
GPG signature fails — ensure you signed export.json after your last edit; re-run signing step
Empty export.json — check that extract_portable_data returns a dictionary, not None
Conclusion
In this lab, you implemented a simplified but realistic GDPR Article 20 data portability workflow. You learned to distinguish portable (user-provided) data from non-portable (internally derived) data, built a Python exporter producing both JSON and CSV formats, secured the export with a GPG digital signature for integrity verification, delivered it via SFTP, and validated the output against a JSON schema. These skills map directly to backend engineering tasks required for GDPR/CIPT-aligned data privacy compliance work.
